<summary>Full PoC test file (copy to <code>programs/paraloom/tests/deactivate_token_strand_test.rs</code>)</summary>

```rust
//! Lane P PoC — `deactivate_validator` strands the validator's dual-stake
//! TOKEN half. Run from the repo root:
//!   cp deactivate_token_strand_test.rs repo/programs/paraloom/tests/
//!   cargo test --manifest-path repo/programs/paraloom/Cargo.toml \
//!       --offline --test deactivate_token_strand_test
//!   rm repo/programs/paraloom/tests/deactivate_token_strand_test.rs
//!
//! Expected (bug present): `deactivate_strands_token_stake` FAILS at the
//! two post-withdraw balance asserts (validator token account short by
//! TOKEN_STAKE, shared vault still holding TOKEN_STAKE); the intermediate
//! asserts PASS and pin the mechanism (token never moved to unbonding).
//! `unregister_returns_token_stake_control` PASSES (positive control).

use anchor_lang::prelude::*;
use anchor_lang::solana_program::program_pack::Pack;
use anchor_lang::{InstructionData, ToAccountMetas};
use paraloom_program::{
    accounts, instruction, ValidatorAccount, MIN_VALIDATOR_STAKE,
};
use solana_program_test::{processor, tokio, ProgramTest, ProgramTestContext};
use solana_sdk::{
    instruction::Instruction, signature::{Keypair, Signer}, transaction::Transaction,
};

mod common;
use common::{
    add_program_data, add_stake_mint, entry, funded_validator,
    init_validator_registry_ix, register_validator_ix, stake_vault_pdas,
    withdraw_unbonded_ix, TEST_TOKEN_FUND,
};

/// Token half of the dual-stake used across these tests (== MIN_TOKEN_STAKE).
const TOKEN_STAKE: u64 = paraloom_program::RECOMMENDED_MIN_TOKEN_STAKE;

async fn send(ctx: &mut ProgramTestContext, signer: &Keypair, ix: Instruction)
    -> std::result::Result<(), solana_program_test::BanksClientError> {
    let blockhash = ctx.get_new_latest_blockhash().await.expect("new blockhash");
    let mut tx = Transaction::new_with_payer(&[ix], Some(&signer.pubkey()));
    tx.sign(&[signer], blockhash);
    ctx.banks_client.process_transaction(tx).await
}

async fn token_balance(ctx: &mut ProgramTestContext, key: Pubkey) -> u64 {
    let raw = ctx.banks_client.get_account(key).await.expect("rpc")
        .expect("token account exists");
    spl_token::state::Account::unpack(&raw.data).expect("unpack token account").amount
}

async fn load_validator(ctx: &mut ProgramTestContext, pda: Pubkey) -> ValidatorAccount {
    let raw = ctx.banks_client.get_account(pda).await.expect("rpc")
        .expect("validator account exists");
    ValidatorAccount::try_deserialize(&mut raw.data.as_slice()).expect("deserialize validator")
}

fn deactivate_ix(program_id: Pubkey, validator_pda: Pubkey, registry_pda: Pubkey, authority: Pubkey) -> Instruction {
    Instruction {
        program_id,
        data: instruction::DeactivateValidator {}.data(),
        accounts: accounts::DeactivateValidator {
            validator_account: validator_pda,
            validator_registry: registry_pda,
            authority,
        }.to_account_metas(None),
    }
}

async fn setup_registry(ctx: &mut ProgramTestContext, program_id: Pubkey, program_data_pda: Pubkey, upgrade_authority: &Keypair, stake_mint: Pubkey) {
    send(ctx, upgrade_authority, init_validator_registry_ix(
        program_id, upgrade_authority.pubkey(), program_data_pda, stake_mint,
    )).await.expect("init registry");
}

async fn register(ctx: &mut ProgramTestContext, program_id: Pubkey, validator: &Keypair, validator_token: Pubkey, stake_mint: Pubkey) {
    send(ctx, validator, register_validator_ix(
        program_id, validator.pubkey(), stake_mint, validator_token,
        MIN_VALIDATOR_STAKE, TOKEN_STAKE,
    )).await.expect("register");
}

/// BUG: after deactivate + unbonding withdraw, the validator's 1_000_000
/// token stake is gone — still sitting in the shared vault, referenced by
/// no account, returnable by no instruction.
#[tokio::test]
async fn deactivate_strands_token_stake() {
    let program_id = paraloom_program::ID;
    let mut pt = ProgramTest::new("paraloom_program", program_id, processor!(entry));
    let (program_data_pda, upgrade_authority) = add_program_data(&mut pt, program_id);
    let stake_mint = add_stake_mint(&mut pt, upgrade_authority.pubkey());
    let (validator, validator_token) = funded_validator(&mut pt, stake_mint);
    let mut ctx = pt.start_with_context().await;

    let (registry_pda, _) = Pubkey::find_program_address(&[b"validator_registry"], &program_id);
    let (validator_pda, _) =
        Pubkey::find_program_address(&[b"validator", validator.pubkey().as_ref()], &program_id);
    let (stake_vault, _) = stake_vault_pdas(program_id);

    setup_registry(&mut ctx, program_id, program_data_pda, &upgrade_authority, stake_mint).await;

    assert_eq!(token_balance(&mut ctx, validator_token).await, TEST_TOKEN_FUND,
        "validator starts with the full baked token fund");

    register(&mut ctx, program_id, &validator, validator_token, stake_mint).await;
    assert_eq!(token_balance(&mut ctx, validator_token).await, TEST_TOKEN_FUND - TOKEN_STAKE,
        "register locks the token half into the shared vault");
    assert_eq!(token_balance(&mut ctx, stake_vault).await, TOKEN_STAKE,
        "vault holds exactly the locked token stake");

    // Admin deactivates the validator (registry authority, normal operation).
    send(&mut ctx, &upgrade_authority,
        deactivate_ix(program_id, validator_pda, registry_pda, upgrade_authority.pubkey()))
        .await.expect("deactivate");

    // SOL half: correctly routed into unbonding (the existing test pins this).
    let acc = load_validator(&mut ctx, validator_pda).await;
    assert!(!acc.is_active, "deactivate must clear is_active");
    assert_eq!(acc.stake_amount, 0, "active SOL stake zeroed on deactivate");
    assert_eq!(acc.unbonding_amount, MIN_VALIDATOR_STAKE, "SOL stake routed into unbonding");
    // TOKEN half: NOT routed — the bug. unregister/slash move it; deactivate
    // leaves token_stake_amount in place and token_unbonding_amount at zero.
    assert_eq!(acc.token_stake_amount, TOKEN_STAKE,
        "BUG? token_stake_amount still holds the full token stake after deactivate");
    assert_eq!(acc.token_unbonding_amount, 0,
        "BUG: token_unbonding_amount is 0 after deactivate — the token half was never routed into unbonding, so withdraw cannot return it");

    // Warp past the unbonding window and withdraw: SOL comes back, tokens don't.
    ctx.warp_to_slot(acc.unbonding_slot).expect("warp to unbonding slot");
    send(&mut ctx, &validator,
        withdraw_unbonded_ix(program_id, validator.pubkey(), stake_mint, validator_token))
        .await.expect("withdraw unbonded stake");

    // PDA is closed — the validator has fully exited.
    let closed = ctx.banks_client.get_account(validator_pda).await.expect("rpc");
    assert!(closed.is_none() || closed.unwrap().lamports == 0, "PDA must be closed after withdraw");
    // ...but the token stake never came back.
    assert_eq!(token_balance(&mut ctx, validator_token).await, TEST_TOKEN_FUND,
        "BUG: validator's token account must be whole again after a full exit (fund minus nothing) — the TOKEN_STAKE tokens are stranded in the vault");
    assert_eq!(token_balance(&mut ctx, stake_vault).await, 0,
        "BUG: shared vault must be empty after the only validator exits — the stranded TOKEN_STAKE tokens are still locked in it, referenced by no account and returnable by no instruction");
}
```

The positive control `unregister_returns_token_stake_control` (same setup, exit via `unregister_validator`) PASSES: `token_unbonding_amount == TOKEN_STAKE` after unregister, and both balances whole after withdraw.
</details>

## Limitations / what this is NOT

- No attacker profit: the tokens are stranded, not stolen — that is why this is Medium, not High/Critical.
- Precondition is the registry authority calling `deactivate` — a documented routine admin operation (validator removal / post-reset reconciliation). It is not a key compromise.
- **Downgrade risk, stated honestly:** triage may rate this Low given the admin precondition and no attacker profit. Counterweight: the trigger is a routine documented operation and the loss is permanent and third-party (the validator's collateral, not the admin's own funds).
- PoC ran on a local `ProgramTest` validator, not against the live devnet program (no devnet transactions were sent).

## Distinctness

- **Not #1625:** different state (`token_stake_amount` / `token_unbonding_amount`, not registry counters `total_active_stake` / `active_validators`), different impact (a validator's token collateral permanently locked, not a quorum halt), different fix, and **no** reset/orphan precondition — it reproduces on a plain active validator. It also survives fix PR #1626 (which adds a new orphan-only instruction and does not touch `deactivate_validator`).
- **Not #1630 / #1631:** same family distinction as above (registry double-decrement, not token accounting).

## Suggested fix (3 lines)

In `deactivate_validator`, mirror `unregister_validator`: move `token_stake_amount` → `token_unbonding_amount`.

---

Payout (USDC): `0xd7cEe56411839319573801D9c0F59d62c9ba39cc`

